In 1985, the American [[funk rock]] band [[War (American band)|War]] recorded a version of "Groovin{{'"}} for their album ''Where There's Smoke''. Upon being issued as a single, their rendition reached number 30 on the U.S. ''[[Billboard (magazine)|Billboard]]'' [[Adult Contemporary (chart)|Adult Contemporary]] chart in the spring of 1985 and number 79 on the ''Billboard'' [[Hot R&B/Hip-Hop Songs|Hot Black Singles]] chart.{{Sfn|Whitburn|1993|p=250}}{{Sfn|Whitburn|2017|p=531}}

In 1996, [[Pato Banton]] recorded a version with the Reggae Revolution that reached number 14 on the [[UK Singles Chart]] in July.{{Sfn|Brown|2000|p=166}} The next month, the cover became a top-ten hit in New Zealand, reaching number four on the [[Recorded Music NZ|RIANZ Singles Chart]] and staying in the top 20 for nine weeks.<ref>{{cite web |title=Pato Banton & The Reggae Revolution – Groovin' (song) |url=https://charts.nz/showitem.asp?interpret=Pato+Banton+%26+The+Reggae+Revolution&titel=Groovin%27&cat=s |access-date=October 27, 2018 |website=charts.nz}}</ref> It was the country's 47th-best-selling single of the year and received a [[Music recording certification|gold]] sales certification for selling over 5,000 copies.<ref>{{cite web |title=End of Year Charts 1996 |url=https://aotearoamusiccharts.co.nz/archive/annual-singles/1996-12-31 |access-date=October 27, 2018 |publisher=[[Recorded Music NZ]]}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |title=Official Top 40 Singles – 6 October 1996 |url=https://nztop40.co.nz/chart/index?chart=3736 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211020043949/https://nztop40.co.nz/chart/index?chart=3736 |url-status=dead |archive-date=October 20, 2021 |access-date=November 19, 2019 |publisher=[[Recorded Music NZ]]}}</ref>

